::ALG2_U03_L01_Q01::
Question ID: ALG2_U03_L01_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.7; MLA.A2.AE.8
Question:
Simplify sqrt(72).
{
= 6sqrt(2)#Correct. 72 = 36 times 2, and sqrt(36) = 6.
~ 36sqrt(2)#This is not fully simplified. Factor the radicand using the greatest perfect-square factor, take the square root of that factor, and leave only the non-square factor under the radical.
~ 3sqrt(8)#This is not fully simplified. Factor the radicand using the greatest perfect-square factor, take the square root of that factor, and leave only the non-square factor under the radical.
~ 8sqrt(9)#This is not fully simplified. Factor the radicand using the greatest perfect-square factor, take the square root of that factor, and leave only the non-square factor under the radical.
}

